3. Coverage Analysis
Coverage Percentage
Based on the Cognitive API Specification and standard conversational bounds, the current coverage is estimated as:

Grammar Recognition: ~35-40% (Relies heavily on brittle prefix and exact-match triggers)
Slot Extraction: ~30% (Captures simple remainder strings after prefixes)
Temporal Extraction: ~10% (Extracts the string directly without normalizing, e.g. "tomorrow" -> "tomorrow")
Entity Extraction: ~15% (Hardcoded to map specific slot names like city and item)
Reference Extraction: ~5% (Only captures pronouns if manually forced into a target slot via grammar rules)
Missing Grammar Rules
The current implementation completely lacks support for:

Arithmetic Expressions: (e.g., 3+3, 15*27)
File & System Operations: (e.g., open notes.txt, rename document.docx)
Rich Temporal Queries: (e.g., what is on my schedule next Friday)
Natural Conversational Idioms: Variations in phrasing break the prefix/exact match rules.
Missing Slot Extraction
Even when intents are recognized, slots are frequently missed:

Quantities/Amounts: No grammar rules extract numbers or units.
Implicit Targets: "remind me" does not extract "me" as the target of the reminder.
Multiple Slots: Prefix rules only support capturing a single trailing string.
Missing Semantic Extraction
There are distinct gaps where a slot successfully extracts, but semantic mapping fails:

Note Content: The take_note intent extracts a content slot, but because content is not mapped in extractors.go, no Entity is populated.
Unmapped Pronouns: The system fails to tag it, this, or that as References unless explicitly placed into a target slot.
4. Architectural Recommendations
Keep Semantic Extraction and Normalization Separate
Maintain a clean pipeline boundary: Grammar -> Slots -> TemporalExtractor -> TemporalNormalizer -> TemporalAnchors.
Delay Compound Intent Detection
Ensure the single-intent pipeline is fully robust before introducing the complexity of parsing multiple intents (e.g. and/then).
Modularize Extractor Implementation
Begin modularizing the extractors.go file before it grows into a monolithic structure.
Recommended future structure:
