5. Recommended Implementation Order (Phase 4B Backlog)
To expand coverage efficiently while adhering to the approved architecture freeze, prioritize Phase 4B implementation in the following order:

Grammar coverage expansion (e.g., regex-based rules, arithmetic)
Slot extraction improvements (e.g., extracting quantities, capturing implicit targets)
Semantic extraction improvements (e.g., mapping note contents, expanding pronoun resolution)
Temporal normalization (e.g., converting "tomorrow" to absolute time)
Natural language variation (e.g., relaxing strict prefix checks)
Compound intent detection (e.g., handling conjunctions in the orchestrator)

## Phase 4B Success Criteria

Understanding Phase 4B will be considered complete when:

✓ Grammar coverage has expanded beyond simple exact/prefix rules.

✓ Slot extraction supports multiple parameters.

✓ Generic entity extraction works independently of specific slot names.

✓ Reference extraction recognizes common pronouns naturally.

✓ Temporal normalization converts natural language into canonical time representations.

✓ The Understanding layer correctly interprets diverse real-world inputs demonstrated through trace audits.

✓ No architectural or schema changes were required.

## Future Expansion

The current implementation uses deterministic extractors.

The extractor architecture is intentionally designed to allow future implementations including:

• Deterministic
• Regex
• Neural
• Hybrid
• LLM-assisted

without modifying the Cognitive API Specification.

Every Phase 4B milestone must conclude with a trace audit.

